  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIHR RIGHT 1: Prevention of epilepsy from birth-related brain injury</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of our program is to examine if a pragmatic, evidenced based and generalisable intrapartum care bundle (includes 4 elements birth companion, intelligent auscultation, electronic medical care record, brain oriented neonatal resuscitation) will reduce birth injury related epilepsy at 18 months of age in three public sector hospitals in India. Imperial is the lead institution. University College London is lead for neonatal aEEG and seizure diagnosis. University of Manchester and Liverpool School for Tropical Medicine are lead for birth companion element of care bundle, University of Oxford is lead for Epilepsy and Veevan Ventures is the coordinating site for the participating sites in India.   Objectives:(1) To examine if a pragmatic, evidenced based and generalisable intrapartum care bundle involving birth companions and empowering mothers will reduce birth injury related epilepsy at 18 months of age in India.(2) If effective, incorporate care bundle into the Labour Room Quality Improvement (LaQshya) programme, for national implementation, thus averting approximately 50,000 epilepsy cases every year in India.(3) Provide opportunities for academic and clinical capacity building in India in midwifery, neonatal/paediatric neurology and epilepsy, and public health.</narrative>
  </description>
